        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ba54465f-f862-5833-8d1b-3f31abe7b52c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: English Water Spaniel, Estonian Hound, American Water Spaniel\n- People: Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer\n- Organizations: Soviet Union national economy ministry, United Kennel Club, American Kennel Club\n\nFacts:\n- The English Water Spaniel is an extinct dog breed, and the last specimen was seen in the 1930s after the breed disappeared in the first part of the 20th century.\n- In 1947, the Soviet Union's national economy ministry required that every country in the Union have its own dog breed, and the Estonian Hound was bred in that context.\n- Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer saved the American Water Spaniel by establishing its breed club and standard.\n- Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer's work led to recognition of the American Water Spaniel by the United Kennel Club and later by the American Kennel Club.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "03b2a1cd-0be6-5714-bc4d-d2e0e8365aea",
        "text": "Page: English Water Spaniel. Sentence: The English Water Spaniel is a breed of dog that has been extinct since the first part of the 20th century, with the last specimen seen in the 1930s.\nPage: Estonian Hound. Sentence: It was bred in 1947 when the Soviet Union's national economy ministry decided that every country in the Union must have its own dog breed.\nPage: American Water Spaniel. Sentence: The breed was saved by Dr. Fred J. Pfeifer, who set up the breed club and standard, and whose work led to recognition for the breed by the United Kennel Club, and later, the American Kennel Club.",
